WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.600 --> 00:00:03.403
[rock music]

00:00:03.470 --> 00:00:06.506
GORDON RAMSAY:
[inaudible],, you are crazy.

00:00:06.573 --> 00:00:07.474
OK.
Lasso.

00:00:07.540 --> 00:00:08.608
GORDON RAMSAY
(VOICEOVER): Over 30

00:00:08.675 --> 00:00:10.443
years of working
as a chef has all

00:00:10.510 --> 00:00:12.078
been leading to this moment--

00:00:12.145 --> 00:00:16.683
catching a Peruvian
cactus worm with a lasso.

00:00:16.750 --> 00:00:20.487
Una, dos, tres.

00:00:20.553 --> 00:00:21.388
Ah.

00:00:21.454 --> 00:00:22.522
Yeah.

00:00:22.589 --> 00:00:24.958
[laughter]

00:00:25.024 --> 00:00:25.992
GORDON RAMSAY: Hey, Haresh.

00:00:26.059 --> 00:00:27.160
I'm going to kill you.

00:00:27.227 --> 00:00:28.728
You gotta get up here first.

00:00:28.795 --> 00:00:32.065
Oh, man.

00:00:32.132 --> 00:00:33.032
Oh!

00:00:33.099 --> 00:00:35.001
[laughter]

00:00:35.068 --> 00:00:35.935
Excuse me, that is not

00:00:36.002 --> 00:00:38.171
funny.

00:00:38.238 --> 00:00:39.806
Be careful.

00:00:39.873 --> 00:00:43.042
GORDON RAMSAY: This
is super dangerous.

00:00:43.109 --> 00:00:44.210
Uno, dos, tres.

00:00:51.084 --> 00:00:52.252
Oh!

00:00:52.318 --> 00:00:53.052
Yeah!

00:00:53.119 --> 00:00:54.788
[laughter]

00:00:59.292 --> 00:01:00.193
Si!

00:01:00.260 --> 00:01:01.294
Si, si, si!

00:01:01.361 --> 00:01:02.595
[inaudible]

00:01:02.662 --> 00:01:03.596
[speaking spanish]

00:01:03.663 --> 00:01:04.998
Hey, good job.

00:01:05.064 --> 00:01:06.166
[laughter]

00:01:07.467 --> 00:01:08.168
Look at that.

00:01:12.205 --> 00:01:13.306
Seriously?

00:01:13.373 --> 00:01:14.707
[bleep]

00:01:14.774 --> 00:01:17.944
[music playing]

00:01:19.913 --> 00:01:20.713
Going to be delicious.

00:01:20.780 --> 00:01:22.315
I'm proud of you.

00:01:22.382 --> 00:01:23.516
[inaudible]

00:01:29.289 --> 00:01:29.989
Ay, yay, yay.

00:01:33.593 --> 00:01:35.862
They're like
giant caterpillars.

00:01:35.929 --> 00:01:37.831
How did he first
learn about these?

00:01:50.276 --> 00:01:51.945
[inaudible] Excellent.

00:01:52.011 --> 00:01:53.112
And how old were
you when you first

00:01:53.179 --> 00:01:54.714
started dangling off
the side of a cliff

00:01:54.781 --> 00:01:55.782
with your dad looking for worms?

00:01:58.785 --> 00:01:59.786
Six or seven.

00:01:59.853 --> 00:02:00.487
Amazing.

00:02:05.892 --> 00:02:08.127
I'm just going to get
them a little bit dry,

00:02:08.194 --> 00:02:09.295
just so it doesn't crackle.

00:02:11.931 --> 00:02:13.099
OK, go.

00:02:13.166 --> 00:02:13.900
[sizzling]

00:02:13.967 --> 00:02:14.834
Whoa!

00:02:14.901 --> 00:02:15.602
[bleep]

00:02:16.503 --> 00:02:17.537
You OK?

00:02:17.604 --> 00:02:19.539
[laughter]

00:02:23.443 --> 00:02:24.844
Oh, bravo!

00:02:24.911 --> 00:02:25.979
[laughter]

00:02:27.013 --> 00:02:27.714
Thank you.

00:02:30.650 --> 00:02:31.351
GORDON RAMSAY: Stop it.

00:02:50.703 --> 00:02:52.605
[laughter]

00:02:55.074 --> 00:02:56.509
It's like a--

00:02:56.576 --> 00:02:59.012
it's like a crispy, uh--

00:02:59.078 --> 00:03:01.381
like a crispy cockroach.

00:03:01.447 --> 00:03:04.183
[laughter]

00:03:05.218 --> 00:03:08.454
[music playing]

00:03:09.656 --> 00:03:11.858
The taste was crispy
to begin with-- fine.

00:03:11.925 --> 00:03:13.259
However, the inside?

00:03:13.326 --> 00:03:14.060
Nah.

00:03:14.127 --> 00:03:15.328
No bueno.

00:03:15.395 --> 00:03:18.464
But this is how they survived
so remotely-- protein

00:03:18.531 --> 00:03:21.067
growing literally in a cactus.

00:03:21.134 --> 00:03:22.135
So an amazing secret,
and a big eye-opener.

